---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CaseStudy from '../../components/case/CaseStudy.astro';
import ModuleMap from '../../components/case/ModuleMap.astro';
import { projectRecords } from '../../data/portfolio';
import { koranco as korancoProject } from '../../data/registry';
import { PUBLIC_LINKS, SITE, caseMeta, SOCIAL_IMAGE } from '../../config/site';

const meta = caseMeta({
  name: korancoProject.name,
  summary: projectRecords.koranco.summary,
  image: '/social/koranco.png',
  imageAlt: 'Koranco Farms — attendance, produce and employee records, drawn as a module map.',
});
const { title, description, image, imageAlt } = meta;
const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'CreativeWork',
  name: 'Koranco Farms MVP',
  description,
  url: new URL('/work/koranco/', Astro.site).href,
  author: { '@type': 'Person', name: SITE.name },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  {title}
  {description}
  {structuredData}
  {image}
  {imageAlt}
  imageWidth={SOCIAL_IMAGE.width}
  imageHeight={SOCIAL_IMAGE.height}
  ogType="article"
>
  <CaseStudy id="koranco">
    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <div style="view-transition-name: artifact-koranco">
        <ModuleMap />
      </div>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="problem">
      <p>
        Farm records were being kept for the office, not for the field. The engagement’s job was to
        find out how production data was actually captured, organised and used — and then to build
        something that survived the conditions it was used in.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three record types came out of that: who was present, what was produced, and who worked
        there. They are the whole scope of the MVP; nothing else is claimed.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="contribution">
      <p>
        I did the software engineering for the three-module MVP during the six-week Ashesi
        Innovation Lab engagement, working alongside the farm-operations side of the project.
      </p>

      <ul class="role-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Offline-first field work</strong> — the modules were built so attendance, produce
          and employee records can be entered where connectivity is poor, rather than only where
          the office is.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Authentication and authorization</strong> — custom authentication with
          role-based access, on FastAPI and PostgreSQL, so a farmhand and a manager do not see the
          same records.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A public face for the farm</strong> — a website built for the business, to make it
          findable and reachable. It is described, not linked: its address is not in the supplied
          record.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="case-note">
        Beyond the stack, the code is not public, so no schema, endpoint or permission rule is
        described here — those would be guesses.
      </p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="decisions">
      <dl class="decision-list">
        <div>
          <dt>Follow the records, not a feature list</dt>
          <dd>
            The engagement’s output was three record types — attendance, produce and employees — so
            the MVP is organised around them rather than around a generic suite of farm features.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Build for the connection the farm has</dt>
          <dd>
            Offline-first was the shape of the product, not a later optimisation: records are
            captured in the field and reconciled afterwards, so a dropped connection does not stop
            the day’s work.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Decide access in the service</dt>
          <dd>
            Custom authentication and role-based authorization live on the backend, next to the
            records they protect, rather than in the interface.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Deliver a working MVP within the engagement</dt>
          <dd>
            Six weeks, through the Ashesi Innovation Lab, delivered as a working MVP rather than a
            design document or a proposal.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="result">
      <p>{projectRecords.koranco.result}</p>

      <dl class="case-states">
        <div>
          <dt>Delivered</dt>
          <dd>
            <strong>Three modules, working.</strong> Attendance, produce and employees, built through
            the six-week Innovation Lab engagement.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Deployment</dt>
          <dd>
            <strong>None evidenced.</strong> No production deployment, farm-side rollout or usage
            figure appears in the record.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="limits">
      <p>{projectRecords.koranco.boundary}</p>

      <ul class="case-evidence case-evidence--missing">
        <li>No public repository, source excerpt or product screenshot</li>
        <li>No production deployment or farm-side adoption reported</li>
        <li>No measured operational outcome — no time saved, error rate or usage figure</li>
        <li>The farm’s website is described but not linked — its address is not in the record</li>
      </ul>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="sources">
      <ul class="case-sources">
        <li>
          <a href="/profile/">Profile and experience record</a>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">This site</span>
          <span>The Jul–Sep 2026 Innovation Lab role this six-week engagement sits inside.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <a href={PUBLIC_LINKS.resume}>Résumé (PDF)</a>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">PDF</span>
          <span>The supplied résumé record this account is drawn from.</span>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="case-sources__plain">Innovation Lab brief</span>
          <span class="case-sources__tag">Not public</span>
          <span>The written project scope. There is no public link to it.</span>
        </li>
      </ul>


    </Fragment>
  </CaseStudy>
</BaseLayout>

